endobj
585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E ( BIT integrates multi-modal biometrics: facial recognition using Python-based AI algorithms, fingerprint scanning, and QR-code verification. Data is encrypted with AES-256 standards, ensuring privacy and security. A cloud-based backend allows scalable storage, while a real-time monitoring dashboard provides automated alerts for unauthorized access. Additional features include attendance tracking, analytics dashboards, and integration with existing HR and event management systems.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
586 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Operational Model & Market Fit:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
587 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (BIT follows a B2B SaaS deployment model, offering subscription tiers and enterprise licenses. Universities, government offices, and event organizers benefit from modular deployment, where smaller organizations can use core features, and larger ones can adopt enterprise analytics and multi-site integration.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
