896 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E ( A Patent Management System is a software solution designed to streamline the management of patents, from submission to approval and tracking. With the increasing need for innovation and intellectual property protection, organizations require efficient systems to manage patent information securely and systematically. This project report presents the design, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive system aimed at simplifying patent management processes, ensuring data integrity, and supporting decision-making. The system integrates modern technologies to provide a scalable, user-friendly, and secure platform, demonstrating practical application of software engineering principles in solving real-world problems. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
897 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (THE WHY BEHIND THIS PROJECT? )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
898 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (In a realm where ideas shape the future, the act of creation is both fragile and profound. Innovators and students alike are full of brilliant ideas ,moments of insight that could transform the way we think, learn, and build. Yet, these ideas often remain vulnerable: creators lack a formal system to document, track, and protect their intellectual property. The absence of a structured patent management process leads to difficulties in ownership verification, delayed approvals, and the risk of unintentional idea loss or misuse. To address this challenge, I built a digital Patent Management System that provides a secure, efficient, and transparent platform for recording, tracking, and managing innovations. The system enables ideas to be formally protected, reduces administrative inefficiencies, promotes innovation, and ensures that intellectual property rights are respected in academic and professional environments. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
899 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (TOOLS OF TRADE )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
900 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 142 0 R
/E (To bring the concept to life, a carefully chosen set of technologies was employed. The backend was built using Elixir and Phoenix, providing scalability, fault tolerance, and real-time capabilities. PostgreSQL was selected for the database, offering reliability and support for complex queries. The frontend leverages HTML, Tailwind CSS, and LiveView, 1 ensuring a responsive, intuitive interface. Each technology was chosen not only for its robustness but also for its alignment with the goals of clarity, efficiency, and maintainability. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
